{
"Among them the peaks to the southwest have the finest woods and valleys.": "4d17ff6ae767",
"And the one with the weathered face and white hair, slumped among them — that is the governor, drunk.": "ba97ab83f1ec",
"And who is the governor? Ou-yang Hsiu of Lu-ling.": "cf68043bb651",
"As for the carriers singing along the road, the walkers resting under the trees, those in front calling and those behind answering, the bent-backed old and the children led by the hand, coming and going without a break — that is the people of Ch'u out walking.": "cd213035402d",
"Before long the evening sun sits on the hills, the shadows of people scatter, the governor goes home and the guests follow.": "b689b013646e",
"But the birds know the joy of hills and woods and do not know the joy of people;": "0b8e180152a1",
"Ch'u is ringed about by hills.": "337acdef93b4",
"Fishing at the stream: the stream is deep and the fish are fat. Brewing the spring water into wine: the spring is fragrant and the wine is clear.": "0f0ad45adb2b",
"Go out at dawn, come back at dusk; the scene differs with each season, and so the joy has no end.": "bf7419d921f2",
"Hill dishes and wild greens set out in a jumble before us — that is the governor's feast.": "cab2e17dacdd",
"The Old Drunkard's mind is not on the wine but on the hills and streams.": "e8c96f3dbcf9",
"The governor comes here to drink with his guests; a little wine and he is drunk, and he is the oldest among them, so he calls himself the Old Drunkard.": "7828cd814ed4",
"The joy of hills and streams is taken in the heart and lodged in the wine.": "4b3ed1b36146",
"The one that looks lush and deeply beautiful from afar is Lang-ya.": "2d1c694cde16",
"The pleasure of the feast at its height is not in strings or pipes: the archer hits, the chess player wins, cups and tallies cross back and forth, people rise and sit and make a din — that is the guests enjoying themselves.": "9b9cf405595a",
"The woods close over in shadow, bird calls come from above and below: the visitors have gone, and the birds are happy.": "314b069d95b7",
"To be drunk and share their joy, and sober to set it down in writing — that is the governor.": "415f0fe263b8",
"Walk six or seven li into the hills and you gradually hear water running; what pours out between two peaks is the Brewing Spring.": "b2203e802ddc",
"When the sun rises the mist in the woods opens; when the clouds come home the caves go dark. This shifting of dark and light is morning and evening in the hills.": "2b97b5c2251e",
"Where the peaks turn and the path bends, a pavilion perches above the spring with its eaves spread like wings: this is the Old Drunkard's Pavilion.": "8a9cf9e39c69",
"Who built the pavilion? A monk of these hills named Chih-hsien.": "b0b19be3fdcb",
"Who named it? The governor, after himself.": "ccd9bb460f1a",
"Wild flowers open with a hidden fragrance; fine trees leaf out into heavy shade; the wind and frost are high and clean; the water drops and the stones emerge. These are the four seasons in the hills.": "cba9233f5c33",
"and the people know the joy of going out with the governor, but do not know that the governor's joy is to take joy in theirs.": "14e16d43989a"
}
